## Context

Intro paragraph 3 (`slides/manuscript/main.tex:146–150`) makes two
promises the body must honour:

> The computable metric is a four-dimension quality score: per-row
> scoring … on accuracy, coherence, provenance, and temporality, with
> citation coverage and **corroboration measured**. The paper counts and
> checks the presence of citations; it does not verify each cited source
> against each cell.

Two problems:

**(a) The four-dimension score is promised but its math is not delivered.**
§3 (`sec:quality`, `:275`) defines the four dimensions only qualitatively.
The author wants an explicit annex section that writes out the maths for
each dimension, aligned to the current code, marked as v0.1 of the
benchmark (to be improved).

**(b) "corroboration measured" is unsupported, and the hedge is misplaced.**
Ground truth (verified 2026-06-15): NO `corroborat*` in any scoring
module — `grep -rli corroborat src/` hits only `plot_exp2_coverage_certainty.py`
(a plot), never `score_*.py`. The code does not measure corroboration.
The very next sentence already concedes "it does not verify each cited
source against each cell" — i.e. the intro contradicts itself. Drop the
corroboration claim; move the citation-hedge sentence out of the intro
into the main text.

## Ground truth (already established — re-confirm, do not re-derive blind)

- Corroboration: absent from `src/aedist/score_*.py`. Author's suspicion
  confirmed → drop the claim.
- The four dimension scorers DO exist and are the source of truth for the
  maths:
  - q1 accuracy (= F1): `src/aedist/score_mechanical.py:score_accuracy`
    + `src/aedist/metrics.py` (`_accuracy`); F1 over matched rows.
  - q2 coherence: `src/aedist/coherence.py` (`check_row_coherence`,
    `check_cross_row_coherence`, `check_aggregate_coherence`) +
    `score_mechanical.py:score_coherence`; the 3-part coherence + run veto
    (see `plot_exp1_reliability.py:51` for the 12-dimension decomposition).
  - q3 provenance: `score_mechanical.py:score_provenance`
    (verifiable vs verified distinction, §3 `:325–331`).
  - q4 temporality: `score_mechanical.py:score_temporality`.

